  "abstract": {
    "value": "An eficient method for the synthesis of chiral tetrahydrocarbazoles (THCs) containing an allene moiety is disclosed, which was established by an enantioconvergent substitution reaction catalyzed by a chiral phosphoric acid. Racemic indolylmethanols bearing the THC motif reacted with Nmethylpyrrole in the presence of the SPINOL-derived chiral phosphoric acid to give the corresponding chiral THCs with allenylsilanes in good yields with high enantioselectivities.",
